From f8f45ecb1d3192ded13853c199d76a730e653d64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "crychic.tan" <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:09:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 146/150] mediatek: mtk_ppe: don't bind WED subflows of PPPoE
 and QinQ frames

The PPE also offloads bridged PPPoE frames, and QinQ frames between
hosts that have untagged traffic as well, as L2 subflows. A subflow
sends its packets with an Ethernet header and an optional VLAN tag, so
once such a flow is offloaded, the PPPoE header or both VLAN tags are
stripped and the DSCP is set to 0. The frames no longer reach the PPPoE
session or their VLAN.

Add a target kernel patch that only binds the subflows of flows that
are forwarded to or received from a WED device for packets with an IP
header right after the MAC header and an optional 802.1Q tag, and leaves
the others to the CPU. Other flows keep the previous behaviour.

The patch is only applied when building for the RAP630W-211G.

Signed-off-by: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
---
 ...ed-subflows-of-pppoe-and-qinq-frames.patch | 45 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12-sonicfi_rap630w_211g/999-2706-net-ethernet-mtk_ppe-do-not-bind-wed-subflows-of-pppoe-and-qinq-frames.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12-sonicfi_rap630w_211g/999-2706-net-ethernet-mtk_ppe-do-not-bind-wed-subflows-of-pppoe-and-qinq-frames.patch b/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12-sonicfi_rap630w_211g/999-2706-net-ethernet-mtk_ppe-do-not-bind-wed-subflows-of-pppoe-and-qinq-frames.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..a458477c76
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12-sonicfi_rap630w_211g/999-2706-net-ethernet-mtk_ppe-do-not-bind-wed-subflows-of-pppoe-and-qinq-frames.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+From: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
+Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: don't bind WED subflows of PPPoE and QinQ frames
+
+The PPE also hashes IPv4/IPv6 packets behind a PPPoE header or behind
+two VLAN tags. __mtk_ppe_check_skb() only takes the VLAN ID of an
+802.1Q tag, so it looks up the L2 flow of such packets with VLAN 0 and
+binds a subflow whenever the two hosts also have an untagged L2 flow.
+For PPPoE that is always the case, as the flow rules of bridged traffic
+only match the MAC addresses. The subflow sends its packets with the L2
+header of the L2 flow, an Ethernet header with an optional VLAN tag and
+the IPv4/IPv6 ethertype, so once it is bound, the PPPoE header or both
+VLAN tags are stripped and the TOS / traffic class is set to 0. The
+frames no longer reach the PPPoE session or their VLAN.
+
+Only bind a subflow for packets with an IP header right after the MAC
+header and an optional 802.1Q tag, the ones mtk_ppe_skb_dsfield() can
+parse, and leave all others to the CPU.
+
+Only do this for flows that are forwarded to or received from a WED
+device, like the other changes to bridged flows. Other flows keep the
+previous behaviour.
+
+Signed-off-by: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
+---
+ drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c |    9 +++++++++
+ 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)
+
+--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
++++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+@@ -954,6 +954,15 @@ void __mtk_ppe_check_skb(struct mtk_ppe *ppe, struct sk_buff *skb, u16 hash)
+ 		u32 *ib2 = &entry->data.bridge.ib2;
+ 		int dsfield = mtk_ppe_skb_dsfield(skb);
+ 
++		/* A subflow sends its packets with the L2 header of its L2
++		 * flow: an Ethernet header with an optional VLAN tag. The PPE
++		 * also hashes packets behind other headers, e.g. PPPoE or QinQ
++		 * frames, which would lose these headers and their DSCP once
++		 * bound. Leave such packets to the CPU.
++		 */
++		if (dsfield < 0)
++			goto out;
++
+ 		*ib2 &= ~MTK_FOE_IB2_DSCP;
+ 		if (dsfield > 0)
+ 			*ib2 |= FIELD_PREP(MTK_FOE_IB2_DSCP, dsfield);
